(FIL-27: negative is true iff the number is below 0; FIL-28 zero iff it is 0; FIL-30 sign is -1, 0 or 1; FIL-31 the worked example.
 Also covers: FIL-28, FIL-30, FIL-31. Three rendered shapes of 'gen leaf
 number sign properties': a negative written as 0 subtract its
 magnitude, zero, and a positive.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
